            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Italian for the excavations, then the Italian for the archaeologist."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: gli ingredienti",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "gli ingredienti — \"the ingredients\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Gli ingredienti sono pochi: farina, uova e latte. There are only a few ingredients: flour, eggs and milk."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Singular l'ingrediente."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ingrediente is a learned borrowing from Latin ingrediēns, the present participle of ingredī \"to go in\" (Lewis & Short): what goes into the dish."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling, explaining and describing at B1."
